  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Consider the following statement.\n\n$-1$ is greater than $-\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nWhat is the negation of this statement?",
  "worked_solution": "Let's denote the given statement as $P.$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\nIt is not true that $-1$ is greater than $-\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nIn other words, $-1$ is *not* greater than $-\\sqrt{2}.$ Therefore, $¬P$ means the following:\n\n$-1$ is **not** greater than $-\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nNote that $P$ is **true,** while $¬P$ is **false.**",
